Package: bt-sync
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Eraser-025 <349610023+Eraser-025@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-pyqt6 | python3-pyqt5, python3-hivex, bluez, pkexec | policykit-1, util-linux, mount, xdg-utils, systemd
Recommends: ntfs-3g, qt6-translations-l10n | qttranslations5-l10n
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Eraser-025/bt-sync
Description: sync Bluetooth pairing keys between Linux and Windows (dual boot)
 bt-sync reads the Bluetooth pairing keys of Linux (BlueZ) and of the Windows
 installation on the same computer, shows the differences and copies the keys
 in the direction you choose, so that your devices work on both systems
 without pairing them again. It includes a tray app, a background scan and a
 backup of the pairing keys.
